“Account Bank Event” means, in respect of an Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank, any of:

the occurrence of an Insolvency Event;

it being or becoming subject to Insolvency Proceedings;

to the extent such Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank is an Electronic Money Institution, an “insolvency event” occurs with respect to it or it becomes subject to “insolvency proceedings”, each as defined in the Electronic Money Regulations 2011/99;

to the extent that such Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank is an Electronic Money Institution as at the date on which it is appointed to act as an Account Bank for the purposes of this Transaction, on any subsequent date it is no longer registered or authorised as an Electronic Money Institution;

the occurrence of an Account Bank Downgrade; or

any event of default (or equivalent event) or breach by the Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank, as the case may be, is continuing in respect of the relevant account bank under the Issuer Account Bank Agreement or any Acknowledgment of Collections Account Declaration of Trust executed by the account bank.

“Available Distribution Amount” means, as at the applicable Cut-Off Date that relates to a Borrowing Base Report, an amount equal to:

for the purposes of determining funds that may be applied towards Initial Purchase Price on any Purchase Date other than a Monthly Payment Date or the payment of Subordinated Settlement Repayment Amount on any Weekly Utilisation Date, the amount (without double counting) equal to the sum of the amount standing to the credit of:

prior to the Issuer Collections Account Effective Date, the Transaction Account and the Pre-Funding Account; and

from (and including) the Issuer Collections Account Effective Date:

the Issuer Collections Account and the Pre-Funding Account; and

any amounts requested by the Issuer under a Senior Utilisation Request or Mezzanine Funding Request pursuant to the terms of any Facility Agreement which will be credited to the Transaction Account:

provided, in each case, that it shall not include any amounts advanced to the Issuer for the purposes of crediting the Pre-Funding Account or Cash Reserve Account; and

in respect of the payment of the Subordinated Settlement Repayment Amount on a Weekly Utilisation Date, on the relevant Weekly Utilisation Date;

in respect of the payment of Initial Purchase Price on a Purchase Date, on the relevant Purchase Date,

for the purposes of calculating the available funds to be applied on any Monthly Payment Date in accordance with the applicable Priority of Payments, the amount (without double counting) equal to the sum of:

the sum of all amounts standing to the credit of the Transaction Account (other than amounts standing to the credit of the Issuer Profit Ledger), Issuer Collections Account and the Cash Reserve Account including, following the occurrence of a Security Enforcement Event, any other proceeds from the enforcement of security over the Purchased Receivables;

any amounts requested by the Issuer under a Senior Utilisation Request, Mezzanine Funding Request pursuant to the terms of any Facility Agreement which will stand to the credit of the Transaction Account for the purpose of financing the acquisition of Receivables on any Monthly Payment Date in accordance with the Priority of Payments, provided that it shall not include any amounts advanced to the Issuer for the purposes of crediting the Pre-Funding Account or Cash Reserve Account;

on any Monthly Payment Date, any amount to be received by the Issuer from a Swap Provider in accordance with any Swap Agreement, other than amounts described in paragraph (iv) below;

any amount to be received by the Issuer from a Swap Provider in accordance with any Swap Agreement which is a Swap Termination Amount which is not required to be applied to purchase a replacement swap transaction and any amount described in clause 15.2 (Premium Received by the Issuer) or clause 15.3 (Termination payment received by the Issuer) of the Cash Management Agreement; plus

in respect of any Monthly Payment Date occurring during the period from the Closing Date to the date that is six months after the Closing Date, amounts advanced under the Subordinated Facility to be applied pursuant to any of items 1 to 19 of the Pre-Enforcement Priority of Payments, and at any other time, amounts requested by the Issuer (or the Servicer acting on its behalf) under a Subordinated Utilisation Request pursuant to the terms of the Subordinated Facility Agreement which will stand to the credit of the Transaction Account.

“Basic Term Modification” means:

any amendment to the Programme Scheduled Termination Date or the Commitments other than:

any explicit right to cancel, reduce, extend or increase the Commitments already included within the terms of the Transaction Documents; or

any explicit right to extend or renew the Programme Scheduled Termination Date included within the Transaction Documents;

any amendment made to the date of maturity or the date of payment of any Senior Facility, any Mezzanine Note or any Subordinated Facility;

any amendment to the currency of any payment under any Transaction Document;

any amendment to or waiver of a Potential Early Amortisation Event, an Early Amortisation Event, a Potential Servicer Termination Event or a Servicer Termination Event (other than any waiver relating to a breach of the Senior Borrowing Base or the Senior Advance Rate Reduction Event Borrowing Base, which shall be a decision solely for the Senior Lenders, and any waiver relating to a breach of the Mezzanine Borrowing Base, which shall be a decision solely for the Mezzanine Note Purchasers);

any amendment to the definition of Senior Repayment Amount that would result in the repayment of any Senior Loan (in whole or in part) on a date earlier than its expected date of repayment;

any amendment to the definition of Mezzanine Redemption Amount that would result in the repayment of any Mezzanine Note (in whole or in part) on a date earlier than its expected date of maturity or payment (as the case may be);

any amendment to the definitions of Most Senior Lender Instruction and Most Senior Lenders;

any amendment to or waiver of any Event of Default or Mezzanine Event of Default provided that any waiver of an Event of Default will be solely at the discretion of the Senior Lenders and any waiver of a Mezzanine Event of Default will be solely at the discretion of the Mezzanine Note Purchasers;

any amendment to or waiver of any Concentration Limit on any date of determination;

any amendment to or waiver of any of the Eligibility Criteria on any date of determination;

any amendment to delete, remove or modify any representation, warranty or undertaking given by the Issuer, the Seller, the Servicer or the Subordinated Lender in a manner which is prejudicial to any Senior Lender or any Mezzanine Note Purchaser;

any amendment to the principal and/or interest on the Senior Facility;

any amendment to the definition of “Mezzanine Advance Rate”;

any amendment to any Priority of Payments;

any amendment to the principal and/or interest on the Mezzanine Notes;

any amendment to the terms providing for the resignation, replacement and appointment of any Transaction Party;

any amendment to the definition of “Change of Control” or any waiver of any Change of Control;

any amendment to the terms of enforcement of any Transaction Security;

any release of any of the Secured Property (other than as explicitly contemplated in the Transaction Documents);

any amendment to Clause 3.41 (Recovering Funding Party and Sharing Payment) of the Master Framework Agreement; or

any amendment to this definition.

“Collections” means, in respect of any Purchased Receivable:

all cash collections and other cash proceeds of the Receivable in respect of the relevant Borrower Agreement, including, without limitation, all finance charges (if any), all VAT (if any) and cash proceeds of any Related Rights;

any proceeds received by the Seller of the Receivable from insurance policies;

any Deemed Collection relating to the Purchased Receivable;

any proceeds from the sale of the Purchased Receivable received by the Issuer from any third party;

any amounts paid to a Collections Account in respect of any Purchased Receivable that becomes a Top-Up Receivable;

any amounts paid to the Issuer by the Swap Provider; and

any Repurchase Price paid to the Issuer by the Seller in respect of the Purchased Receivable in connection with any permitted repurchase of the Purchased Receivable.

“Indebtedness” means, with respect to any Person at any date, any indebtedness for or in respect of:

moneys borrowed and debit balances at banks or other financial institutions;

any acceptance under any acceptance credit or bill discounting facility (or dematerialised equivalent);

any note purchase facility or the issue of bonds, notes, debentures, loan stock or any similar instrument;

the amount of any liability in respect of any lease or hire purchase contract which would, in accordance with applicable accounting principles, be treated as a balance sheet liability;

receivables sold or discounted (other than any receivables to the extent they are sold on a non-recourse basis);

any treasury transaction (and, when calculating the value of that treasury transaction, only the marked to market value (or, if any actual amount is due as a result of the termination or close-out of that treasury transaction, that amount) shall be taken into account);

any derivative transaction entered into in connection with protection against or benefit from fluctuation in any rate or price (and, when calculating the value of any derivative transaction, only the marked to market value (or, if any actual amount is due as a result of the termination or close-out of that treasury transaction, that amount) shall be taken into account);

any counter-indemnity obligation in respect of a guarantee, indemnity, bond, standby or documentary letter of credit or any other instrument issued by a bank or financial institution;

any amount raised by an issue of redeemable shares;

any amount of any liability under an advance or deferred purchase agreement if one of the primary reasons behind entering into the agreement is to raise finance;

any amount raised under any other transaction (including any forward sale or purchase, sale and sale back or sale and leaseback agreement) having the commercial effect of a borrowing; and

the amount of any liability in respect of any guarantee or indemnity for any of the items referred to in paragraphs (a) to (k) above.

“Insolvency Event” means, with respect to a Person, that Person:

is dissolved (other than pursuant to a solvent consolidation, amalgamation or merger);

becomes insolvent or is unable to pay its debts or fails or admits in writing its inability generally to pay its debts as they become due;

makes a general assignment, arrangement or composition with or for the benefit of its creditors;

institutes or has instituted against it, by a regulator, supervisor or any similar official with primary insolvency, rehabilitative or regulatory jurisdiction over it in the jurisdiction of its incorporation or organisation or the jurisdiction of its head or home office, a proceeding seeking a judgment of insolvency or bankruptcy or any other relief under any bankruptcy or insolvency law or other similar law affecting creditors’ rights, or a petition is presented for its winding-up or liquidation by it or such regulator, supervisor or similar official;

has instituted against it a proceeding seeking a judgment of insolvency or bankruptcy or any other relief under any bankruptcy or insolvency law or other similar law affecting creditors’ rights, or a petition is presented for its winding-up or liquidation, and, in the case of any such proceeding or petition instituted or presented against it, such proceeding or petition is instituted or presented by a person or entity not described in paragraph (d) above and:

results in a judgment of insolvency or bankruptcy or the entry of an order for relief or the making of an order for its winding-up or liquidation; or

is not dismissed, discharged, stayed or restrained in each case within 30 days of the institution or presentation thereof;

has a resolution passed for its winding-up, official management or liquidation (other than pursuant to a solvent consolidation, amalgamation or merger);

seeks or becomes subject to the appointment of an administrator, provisional liquidator, conservator, receiver, trustee, custodian or other similar official for it or for all or substantially all its assets (other than, for so long as it is required by law or regulation not to be publicly disclosed, any such appointment which is to be made, or is made, by a person or entity described in paragraph (d) above);

has a secured party take possession of all or substantially all its assets or has a distress, execution, attachment, sequestration or other legal process levied, enforced or sued on or against all or substantially all its assets and such secured party maintains possession, or any such process is not dismissed, discharged, stayed or restrained, in each case within 30 days thereafter;

causes or is subject to any event with respect to it which, under the applicable laws of any jurisdiction, has an analogous effect to any of the events specified in paragraphs (a) to (h) above; or

takes any action in furtherance of, or indicating its consent to, approval of, or acquiescence in, any of the foregoing acts.

“Insolvency Proceedings” means, with respect to any person, any corporate action, legal proceedings, petition or step is taken in relation to:

the suspension of payments, a moratorium of any indebtedness, winding-up, dissolution, administration or reorganisation (by way of voluntary arrangement, scheme of arrangement or otherwise);

a composition, compromise, assignment or arrangement with any creditor;

the appointment of a liquidator, receiver, administrative receiver, administrator, examiner, compulsory manager or other similar officer in respect of such person or any of its assets;

enforcement of any Encumbrance over any of its assets; or

any analogous procedure or step is taken in any jurisdiction,

in each case, excluding any winding-up petition which is frivolous or vexatious and is discharged, stayed or dismissed within 30 days of commencement.

“Legal Reservations” means

the principle that equitable or discretionary remedies may be granted or refused at the discretion of a court and the limitation of enforcement by laws relating to insolvency, reorganisation and other laws generally affecting the rights of creditors;

the time barring of claims under the Limitation Acts, the possibility that an undertaking to assume liability for or indemnify a person against non-payment of UK stamp duty may be void and defences of set-off or counterclaim;

the principle that in certain circumstances Security granted by way of fixed charge may be recharacterised as a floating charge or that Security purported to be constituted by an assignment may be recharacterised as a charge;

the principle that any provision for the payment of compensation or additional interest imposed pursuant to any relevant agreement may be held to be unenforceable on the grounds that it is a penalty and thus void;

the principle that an English court may not give effect to a provision dealing with the cost of litigation where the litigation is unsuccessful or the court itself has made an order for costs;

the principle that the creation or purported creation of Security over any contract or agreement which is subject to a prohibition on transfer, assignment, assignation or charging may be void, ineffective or invalid and may give rise to a breach of the contract or agreement over which such security has been granted;

the principle that the legality, validity, binding nature or enforceability of any Transaction Security which is not governed by the laws of the jurisdiction where the asset or assets purported to be secured under the relevant Transaction Security is situated may be flawed;

similar principles, rights and defences under the laws of any relevant jurisdiction; and

any other matters which are set out as qualifications or reservations as to matters of law of general application in the Legal Opinions.

“Material Adverse Effect” means, any of the following events or circumstances:

a material adverse effect on the collectability of the Receivables taken as a whole or any significant portion thereof;

a material adverse effect on the ability of the Seller, the Servicer, the Issuer, or the Subordinated Lender to perform any of its material obligations under the Transaction Documents to which it is a party;

subject to the Legal Reservations (which are complied with in the manner and at that times required by law or by any Transaction Security), a material adverse effect on the legality, validity or enforceability of any of the Transaction Documents (including, without limitation, the validity, enforceability or priority of any of the Security Interests granted under them);

a material adverse effect on the business, assets or financial condition of the Seller, Servicer or Subordinated Lender; or

a material adverse effect on the interests, rights or remedies of the Issuer, any Senior Lender or any Mezzanine Note Purchaser under or with respect to:

any of the Transaction Documents; or

the Purchased Receivables taken as a whole or any significant portion thereof.

“Mezzanine Funding Date” means, the date determined, as follows:

in respect of the first Mezzanine Funding Request delivered on the Signing Date, the Closing Date;

in respect of any Mezzanine Funding Request delivered on the Business Day prior to a Monthly Investor Reporting Date, the immediately succeeding Monthly Payment Date; and

in respect of any Mezzanine Funding Request delivered on a weekly basis, the Weekly Utilisation Date;

in each case, provided that (i) the relevant Conditions Precedent to Utilisation in respect of that date have been satisfied in full; and (ii) no Mezzanine Funding Date shall fall on the first Business Day of any week.

“MezzanineNERB Aggregate Excess Concentration Amount” means, as at any date of determination following (and including) the NERB Aggregate Excess Concentration Applicable Date, the amount equal to the aggregate of:

the Adjusted Loan Terms Near Prime Borrowers Excess Concentration Amount;

the Adjusted Loan Terms Prime Borrowers Excess Concentration Amount;

the Direct Debit/Push Payments Excess Concentration Amount;

the Maximum Average Weighted Remaining Term Excess Concentration Amount;

the Push Payments Excess Concentration Amount;

the Single Employer Partner Excess Concentration Amount;

the Subprime Borrowers Excess Concentration Amount;

the Top Five Employer Partner Excess Concentration Amount; and

the Weighted Average APR Excess Concentration Amount.

“Mezzanine Redemption Amount” means the amount, on any Monthly Payment Date, equal to:

if the Revolving Period is continuing (other than in any circumstance described in sub-paragraphs (e) or (f) below), the amount (if any) by which the aggregate Mezzanine Principal Amount Outstanding of the Mezzanine Note as at the most recent Funding Date or Monthly Payment Date, as applicable, (after taking account of any anticipated redemptions or Mezzanine Utilisations on the Monthly Payment Date) exceeds the Mezzanine Borrowing Base as at the immediately preceding Cut-Off Date;

any Mezzanine Advance Rate Reduction Percentage Redemption Amount that is payable on that date;

if the Revolving Period has ended but prior to the Final Maturity Date (other than in any circumstance described in sub-paragraphs (d), (e) and (f) below), the amount available to redeem the Mezzanine Notes in full (together with any accrued interest) as at the Monthly Payment Date after satisfaction in full of all amounts ranking in priority to payment of principal in respect of the Mezzanine Notes in the applicable Priority of Payments;

in respect of the Final Maturity Date or following the occurrence of a Mezzanine Event of Default or any mandatory redemption required under Mezzanine Note Condition 4.11 (Mandatory Redemption on a Mezzanine Event of Default) or Mezzanine Note Condition 4.13 (Mandatory Redemption on occurrence of a Subordinated Event of Default or early redemption of the Subordinated Loan) of the Mezzanine Facility Agreement, the aggregate Mezzanine Principal Amount Outstanding of the Mezzanine Notes (together with any accrued interest and Break Costs, if applicable) as at the Monthly Payment Date;

if it is unlawful for any Mezzanine Note Purchaser to continue to participate in the Mezzanine Facilities, unlawful for the Issuer to perform or comply with any of its obligations under a Mezzanine Note or the Transaction Documents or if there is a redemption due to tax, the aggregate Mezzanine Principal Amount Outstanding of the affected Mezzanine Note (together with any accrued interest) as at the Monthly Payment Date; and

in respect of any Mezzanine Optional Redemption of the Mezzanine Note, the Mezzanine Note Reduction Amount as at the Monthly Payment Date.

“Perfection Event” means any Early Amortisation Event, other than:

any event occurring under paragraph 1(a) (Performance Ratios/Triggers) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement;

any event occurring under paragraph 1(b) (Payment not by Salary Deduction) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement;

any event occurring under paragraph 1(c) (Senior Borrowing Base) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement;

any event occurring under paragraph 1(d) (Cash Reserve) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement as a result of the Cash Reserve being less than the Cash Reserve Target Amount on any Monthly Payment Date, solely on account of there not being sufficient Available Distribution Amount on that date to replenish the Cash Reserve pursuant to the relevant Priority of Payments, rather than any failure to fund the Cash Reserve from the proceeds of any Subordinated Advance in connection with an increase to the Senior Principal Amount Outstanding;

on any date from and including the date that is six months from the Closing Date, any event occurring under paragraph 1(e) (Excess Spread) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement;

any event occurring under paragraph 1(f) (Senior Borrowing Base) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement;

any event occurring under paragraph 6(e) (Change of Control) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement; or

any event occurring under paragraph 8(c) (Issuer Account Bank Event) of Schedule 4 (Early Amortisation Events) to the Master Framework Agreement.

“Permitted Modification” means any amendment or modification:

provided that any amendments or modifications requested by [PARTY_NAME] and approved by Latham & Watkins LLP on or prior to the Closing Date shall constitute Permitted Modifications.

which is of a minor or technical nature or to correct a manifest error;

required to comply with any law, regulation or rules and guidance from the FCA, ICO or other regulator or any trade body applicable to the Sellers from time to time;

which imposes tighter or more conservative credit criteria and is otherwise not adverse in any respect to the interests of the Funders;

made with the consent of the Facility Agent (acting on the instructions of each Senior Lender and each Mezzanine Funding Agent) and the Security Trustee (acting on the instructions of the Instructing Creditor) (not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed); or

that is a Receivable Payment Date Change,

“Pre-Approved Agent” means, each of:

Capquest Debt recovery Limited;

Blenheim Chalcot IT Services India Pvt Ltd.;

OPOS Limited; and

any other agent approved in writing by the Facility Agent.

“Qualifying Senior Lender” means a Senior Lender that is:

beneficially entitled to interest payable to that Senior Lender in respect of the relevant Senior Advance and is:

a Senior Lender which is (or was at the time the relevant Senior Advance was made) a bank (as defined for the purpose of section 879 of the ITA) and is within the charge to United Kingdom corporation tax in respect of any payments of interest made in respect of that Senior Advance (or would be within such charge in respect of such payments but for section 18A of the CTA);

a Senior Lender which is:

a company resident in the United Kingdom for United Kingdom tax purposes;

a company not so resident in the United Kingdom but which carries on a trade in the United Kingdom through a permanent establishment and the whole of any interest payable in respect of that Senior Advance falls to be brought into account in computing its chargeable profits (within the meaning of section 19 of the CTA) by reason of Part 17 of the CTA; or

a partnership, each member of which is a person falling within (A) or (B) above or a person or body mentioned in section 936 of the ITA;

a Treaty Senior Lender; or

a building society (as defined for the purpose of section 880 of the ITA) making a Senior Advance.

“Receivable Payment Date Change” means, in respect of any Receivable and its related Consumer Loan, a change of the calendar date on which the scheduled instalment payment date occurs in accordance with the terms of the Borrower Agreement:

to correct an operational, administrative or technical issue raised by the Employer or the Servicer;

where the Employer restructures payroll;

at the request of the Borrower, provided that:

the Employee makes the request as a result of a termination of their employment with the Employer Partner;

the relevant Consumer Loan is not in arrears; and

the requested amended payment date is within 15 calendar days of the previously scheduled payment date; or

to implement payment holidays that are provided in accordance with FCA industry guidance.

“Related Rights” means, in respect of any Receivable:

all deposits, guarantees, rights under any insurance policy written for the benefit of the Seller, indemnities, warranties and other agreements or arrangements of whatever character from time to time supporting or securing payment of that Receivable, to the extent transferable in accordance with their terms and under applicable law without the consent of any party other than the Seller;

all rights to receive and obtain payment under the Borrower Agreement and/or the Employer Partner Service Agreement relating to the Receivable (including, without limitation, any right to demand, sue for, recover, receive and give receipts for payment of any amount or any other right to enforce against the relevant Borrower or an Employer Partner in so far as it relates to the Receivable);

any contractual rights the Seller may have to enforce, or giving rise to a cause of action in respect of, any Purchased Receivable, which may exist as at the origination date of the Borrower Agreement or at any time in the future;

any contractual rights, or cause of action, the Seller may have against an Employer Partner under an Employer Partner Service Agreement in so for as it relates to the Receivable and any proceeds relating to the Receivable received from the Employer Partner (including, without limitation, any recoveries from default interest and losses corresponding to the Receivable); and

all proceeds (including, any Collections), however arising, of the payment or repayment, sale or other disposal (including for debt management purposes) or enforcement of, or dealing with, decree or judgment relating to the Receivable and any pledge, retention of title or other security for its payment.

“Sanctioned Person” means, at any time:

any person listed in any Sanctions-related list of designated persons maintained by the Office of Foreign Assets Control of the U.S. Department of the Treasury, the U.S. Department of State, the United Nations Security Council, Her Majesty’s Treasury of the United Kingdom, the European Union, any EU member state or any other relevant sanctions authority;

any person that is, or is part of, a government of a Sanctioned Country;

any person operating, organised or resident in a Sanctioned Country;

any person owned or controlled, or acting on behalf of any person falling within sub paragraphs (a), (b) or (c) above; or

any person otherwise targeted under any Sanctions.

“Seller Documentation and Policies” means, in relation to the Seller, each of the documents uploaded to the Data Room titled as follows and uploaded to the Data Room by no later than the Data Room Cut-Off Date:

in each case, as may be amended, supplemented or varied from time to time at the discretion of the Seller, subject to the prior written consent of the Facility Agent (acting on the instructions of each of the Senior Lenders and the Mezzanine Funding Agents) unless such amendment, supplement or variation is a Permitted Modification.

