“Senior Repayment Amount” means the amount, on any Monthly Payment Date, equal to:

if the Revolving Period is continuing (other than in any circumstance described in sub-paragraphs (d) or (e) below), the amount (if any) by which the Senior Principal Amount Outstanding as at the immediately preceding Cut-Off Date (after taking account of any anticipated repayments of Senior Advances on the Monthly Payment Date) exceeds the Senior Borrowing Base as at the immediately preceding Cut-Off Date; or

if the Termination Date has occurred but prior to the Final Maturity Date (other than in any circumstance described in sub-paragraphs (c), (d) and (e) below), the amount available to redeem the Senior Loans in full (together with any accrued interest) as at the Monthly Payment Date after satisfaction in full of all amounts ranking in priority to payment of principal in respect of the Senior Facility in the applicable Priority of Payments;

in respect of the Final Maturity Date or following the occurrence of an Event of Default or any mandatory redemption required under clause 7.8 (Mandatory repayment following the occurrence of a Mezzanine Event of Default, Subordinated Event of Default, early redemption of the Mezzanine Note or early repayment of the Subordinated Loan) of the Senior Facility Agreement, the Senior Principal Amount Outstanding (together with any accrued interest and Break Costs, if applicable) as at the Monthly Payment Date;

if it is unlawful for any Senior Lender to continue to participate in the Senior Loan, unlawful for the Issuer to perform or comply with any of its obligations under the Senior Facility or the Transaction Documents, or if there is a redemption due to tax, the Senior Principal Amount Outstanding (together with any accrued interest) as at the Monthly Payment Date; and

in respect of any Senior Voluntary Prepayment, the Senior Reduction Amount as at the Monthly Payment Date.

“Subordinated Settlement Date Conditions” means, in respect of any Business Day during the Revolving Period that the Servicer wishes to deem a Subordinated Settlement Date, the conditions that must be satisfied on that date, as follows:

other than the initial Subordinated Settlement Date in the Revolving Period, the proposed Subordinated Settlement Date must not occur in the period between a Monthly Servicer Reporting Date (exclusive) to but excluding a Monthly Payment Date;

no Early Amortisation Event has occurred and is continuing as at that date (without taking account of any remedy or cure period at that time), unless waived in accordance with Clause 3.28 (Waiver of Servicer Termination Event, Early Amortisation Event, Event of Default or Mezzanine Event of Default) of the Master Framework Agreement;

a duly completed Borrowing Base Report is delivered to the Facility Agent on that date in accordance with clauses 6.1 and 6.2 (Borrowing Base Report) of the Servicing Agreement, recording compliance with the Senior Borrowing Base and the Mezzanine Borrowing Base on that Subordinated Settlement Date (after taking account of any increase or decrease to the aggregate Principal Amount Outstanding of the Senior Facility and the Mezzanine Notes that day); and

on any Subordinated Settlement Date, any withdrawal from any Issuer Account (other than the Pre-Funding Account) for the purpose of paying the Subordinated Settlement Repayment Amount to the Subordinated Lender, shall not cause the Issuer to have an Available Distribution Amount which is insufficient to pay amounts due and payable at paragraphs (1) to (19) (inclusive) of the Pre-Enforcement Priority of Payments on the next Monthly Payment Date.

“Tangible Net Worth” means, in respect of [PARTY_NAME], as at the relevant date of determination and each as determined in accordance with the Accounting Principles and reported in Servicer, Seller, Collections Account Trustee and Subordinated Lender’s most recent audited financial statements or periodic management accounts, an amount equal to the sum of (without double counting):

the aggregate value of the book equity of Servicer, Seller, Collections Account Trustee and Subordinated Lender and its consolidated subsidiaries (which, for the avoidance of doubt, shall not give credit to any intangible assets);

the principal amount outstanding and any accrued interest of the loan advanced to [PARTY_NAME] by Salary Direct Holdings Limited;

the principal amount outstanding and any accrued interest of the loan advanced by ELQ Investors IV Ltd to Servicer, Seller, Collections Account Trustee and Subordinated Lender;

any subordinated debt issued by the Issuer under the Subordinated Facility Agreement with a maturity past or concurrent with the Final Maturity Date;

any deferred revenue; and

any undrawn amount under any committed facility provided by any shareholder of [PARTY_NAME] or any other member of the Seller Group that may be applied towards general corporate purposes which is unconditional and may not be cancelled by the lender.

“UK Securitisation Rules” means:

in each case, as may be further amended, supplemented or replaced, from time to time.

any applicable UK Binding Technical Standards made under the UK Securitisation Regulation;

any relevant standstill decisions, guidance and policy statements relating to the application of the UK Securitisation Regulation (or any binding technical standards) published by the Prudential Regulation Authority and/or the Financial Conduct Authority (or their successors);

