“calendar year” means any 12-month period starting, as applicable:

on the Closing Date; or

on the anniversary of the Closing Date;

“continuing” means:

in respect of an Early Amortisation Event, Potential Early Amortisation Event, Insolvency Event, Servicer Termination Event, Potential Servicer Termination Event, Potential Event of Default and Event of Default, that the relevant event has not been waived by the Facility Agent acting on a Most Senior Lender Instruction;

in respect of a Mezzanine Event of Default or Potential Mezzanine Event of Default, that the relevant event has not been waived by the Mezzanine Funding Agent acting on the instructions of the Mezzanine Note Purchasers; or

in any case where a cure period or remedy period is provided for in the Transaction Documents, the relevant event has not been otherwise cured or remedied in a manner expressly set out in the Transaction Documents for the cure or remedy of such event prior to the expiry of the relevant cure period or remedy period;

“control” means:

where a person (“P”) is treated as having control of a company (“C”) if P:

direct or indirect control over C’s affairs;

exercises;

is able to exercise; or

is entitled to acquire,

in particular, P is treated as having control of C if P possesses or is entitled to acquire:

more than 50% of the share capital or issued share capital of C;

more than 50% of the voting power in C;

so much of the issued share capital of C as would, on the assumption that the whole of the income of C were distributed among the participators, entitle P to receive more than 50% of the amount so distributed; or

such rights as would entitle P, in the event of the winding up of C or in any other circumstances, to receive more than 50% of the assets of C which would then be available for distribution among the participators;

any rights that P or any other person has as a loan creditor are to be disregarded for the purposes of the assumption in paragraph (ii)(C) above; and

if two or more persons together, pursuant to an agreement or understanding (whether formal or informal), actively co-operate to obtain or consolidate control, either directly or indirectly, and satisfy any of the conditions in paragraphs (i) or (ii), they are treated as having control of C.
